-## Features
+## Operations (simple → complex)
 
-- **Earthmoving** — excavator + dump truck, distributions, cost, emissions, fleet comparison
-- **Concreting** — dual-cycle RMC (truck mixer + placing) with site buffer; methods: buggy / crane bucket / pump
-- Shared result tabs: Ringkasan, Perbandingan, queueing insights
-- Illustrations and Indonesian/English learning copy
+1. **Earthmoving** — excavator + dump truck
+2. **Bricklaying** — helper + mason + buffers
+3. **Concreting / RMC** — truck mixer + placing (buggy / crane bucket / pump)
+4. **Tower crane** — multi-front, single server, priority
+5. **Asphalt paving** — plant + truck + paver + rollers
+6. **Precast plant** — form + crew + crane + cure slots
+
+Shared result views: ringkasan, perbandingan fleet (on demand), queueing insights, cost & emissions. Illustrations and Indonesian learning copy.
+
+This is a **classroom model**, not a field design tool.
+
+## Classroom / public lecture
+
+Simulation runs **in the browser**. Hundreds of students do not load the server.
+
+On the **SiklOps-web** Vercel project (this repo, not Parade Tim Kerja):
+
+1. Set `DATABASE_URL` to the same Neon/Postgres URL already used by Parade Tim Kerja (or another Neon database). Redeploy. Check `/statistik` — it should say the backend is Neon.
+2. Leave `VITE_AUTH_ENABLED` unset (login stays off). Set `true` only if you intentionally want Google/X sign-in.
+3. No student accounts are required.
+
+Privacy: a random browser id is stored locally and visit/simulation counts are aggregated. No names or emails unless you turn auth on.
 
